---
import { questions } from '../lib/self-check.mjs';
import { url } from '../lib/paths';

const symptomQuestion = questions.find(question => question.id === 'symptoms');
const symptomOptions = symptomQuestion.options.filter(([id]) => !['none', 'all', 'unsure'].includes(id));
const summaryOptions = symptomQuestion.options.filter(([id]) => ['none', 'all', 'unsure'].includes(id));
---

<section class="symptom-product-guide" aria-labelledby="symptom-guide-title">
  <form id="symptom-product-form" class="symptom-product-form" novalidate>
    <fieldset>
      <legend id="symptom-guide-title">When you are in contact with fragrances (skin, air, clothes)...which of these have you noticed?</legend>
      <p>Select every question that is true for you. These symptoms have many possible causes. This tool cannot identify an allergy, diagnose a condition, or prove that fragrance caused a symptom.</p>
      <div class="symptom-question-list">
        {symptomOptions.map(([value, label]) => <label><input type="checkbox" name="symptoms" value={value}/><span>{label}</span></label>)}
      </div>
      <div class="symptom-question-list symptom-question-list--quiet">
        {summaryOptions.map(([value, label]) => <label><input type="checkbox" name="symptoms" value={value}/><span>{label}</span></label>)}
      </div>
      <p id="symptom-product-error" class="check-error" role="alert" hidden>Select at least one response to see practical areas to review.</p>
      <button class="button" type="submit">Show practical product areas to review <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
    </fieldset>
  </form>

  <section id="symptom-product-result" class="symptom-product-result" hidden aria-labelledby="symptom-product-result-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your practical next step</p>
    <h2 id="symptom-product-result-title" tabindex="-1">Product areas you could review first</h2>
    <p>This is a source-control checklist, not treatment advice. It suggests where optional added scent may be easiest to remove; it does not say a product caused your symptoms or guarantee that changing it will improve them.</p>
    <aside id="symptom-urgent-note" class="notice" hidden><strong>Breathing symptoms need care.</strong> Cough, wheeze, chest tightness, or shortness of breath can have many causes. If symptoms are happening now or worsening, seek prompt medical advice; severe breathing difficulty, throat swelling, or fainting needs emergency help.</aside>
    <div id="symptom-no-match" class="notice" hidden><strong>No symptom pattern selected.</strong> You can still reduce optional added scent one category at a time, starting with products designed to scent the air.</div>
    <div class="symptom-path-grid">
      <article data-symptom-path="air"><span aria-hidden="true">↝</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Air &amp; shared spaces</p><h3>Pause products made to scent the air</h3><p>Review plug-ins, room sprays, diffusers, incense, candles and wax melts first. Replace odour-masking with source control and appropriate ventilation.</p><a href={url('guides/fragrance-free-starter-toolkit/#toolkit-step-01')}>Review air-care changes →</a></div></article>
      <article data-symptom-path="skin"><span aria-hidden="true">✦</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Skin &amp; body</p><h3>Check products that stay on skin</h3><p>Review moisturiser, sunscreen, deodorant, perfume and hand cream before rinse-off products. Choose the exact fragrance-free version and check the current ingredient list.</p><a href={url('directory/?category=Skin+%26+Body')}>Browse skin &amp; body options →</a></div></article>
      <article data-symptom-path="fabrics"><span aria-hidden="true">⌁</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Laundry &amp; fabrics</p><h3>Remove scent from clothes and bedding</h3><p>Review detergent, fabric softener, dryer sheets and scent beads. Fragrance on fabrics can be a continuing source after washing.</p><a href={url('directory/?category=Home+%26+Laundry&q=laundry')}>Browse laundry options →</a></div></article>
      <article data-symptom-path="cleaning"><span aria-hidden="true">⌂</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Cleaning routine</p><h3>Swap sprays and large-surface cleaners</h3><p>Review floor, bathroom, kitchen and dishwashing products. Follow product labels, use ventilation where appropriate, and never mix cleaning chemicals.</p><a href={url('directory/?category=Home+%26+Laundry&q=cleaner')}>Browse cleaning options →</a></div></article>
      <article data-symptom-path="hair"><span aria-hidden="true">〰</span><div><p class="eyebrow">Hair &amp; personal care</p><h3>Check routine products close to the face</h3><p>Review shampoo, conditioner, dry shampoo, styling sprays and body spray. These products may be used near the nose, eyes and airways.</p><a href={url('directory/?category=Haircare')}>Browse haircare options →</a></div></article>
    </div>
    <p class="symptom-clinician-note">For persistent, recurrent, or worrying symptoms, discuss what you noticed with a healthcare professional. Bring the product name, ingredient label, timing, and any other possible exposures. Do not deliberately re-expose yourself or perform a home allergy test.</p>
    <div class="symptom-result-actions"><a class="button" href={url('guides/fragrance-free-starter-toolkit/')}>Use the full starter toolkit →</a><a class="text-link" href={url('evidence/')}>Read the evidence →</a></div>
  </section>

  <details class="symptom-source-context">
    <summary>Why this page is cautious</summary>
    <p>Fragrance and other cosmetic ingredients can trigger allergic reactions in some people, and symptoms can have many other causes. The FDA advises reading the ingredient panel, avoiding ingredients you know or suspect you react to, and speaking with a healthcare professional about suspected reactions. A “fragrance-free” claim does not guarantee that a product will suit everyone.</p>
    <p><a href="https://www.fda.gov/cosmetics/cosmetic-ingredients/allergens-cosmetics">FDA: Allergens in Cosmetics ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.fda.gov/cosmetics/cosmetic-ingredients/fragrances-cosmetics">FDA: Fragrances in Cosmetics ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/anaphylaxis/">NHS: Anaphylaxis and emergency symptoms ↗</a></p>
  </details>
</section>

<script>
  const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#symptom-product-form');
  const result = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#symptom-product-result');
  if (form && result) {
    const inputs = Array.from(form.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="symptoms"]'));
    const error = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#symptom-product-error')!;
    const urgent = result.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#symptom-urgent-note')!;
    const noMatch = result.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#symptom-no-match')!;
    const paths: Record<string, string[]> = {
      air: ['headache', 'eyes', 'nose', 'throat', 'cough', 'breathing', 'nausea', 'dizziness', 'concentration'],
      skin: ['skin', 'eyes'],
      fabrics: ['skin', 'nose', 'eyes', 'throat'],
      cleaning: ['eyes', 'nose', 'throat', 'cough', 'breathing'],
      hair: ['headache', 'eyes', 'nose', 'throat', 'skin'],
    };
    form.addEventListener('change', event => {
      const input = event.target as HTMLInputElement;
      if (!input.matches('input[name="symptoms"]')) return;
      if (input.checked && ['none', 'all', 'unsure'].includes(input.value)) inputs.forEach(item => { if (item !== input) item.checked = false; });
      if (input.checked && !['none', 'all', 'unsure'].includes(input.value)) inputs.filter(item => ['none', 'all', 'unsure'].includes(item.value)).forEach(item => item.checked = false);
      error.hidden = true;
    });
    form.addEventListener('submit', event => {
      event.preventDefault();
      const selected = inputs.filter(input => input.checked).map(input => input.value);
      if (!selected.length) { error.hidden = false; inputs[0].focus(); return; }
      const hasSymptom = selected.includes('all') || selected.some(value => !['none', 'unsure', 'all'].includes(value));
      result.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-symptom-path]').forEach(card => {
        const matches = selected.includes('all') || (hasSymptom && paths[card.dataset.symptomPath!].some(value => selected.includes(value)));
        card.hidden = !matches;
      });
      noMatch.hidden = hasSymptom;
      urgent.hidden = !selected.includes('all') && !selected.some(value => ['cough', 'breathing'].includes(value));
      result.hidden = false;
      result.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#symptom-product-result-title')!.focus();
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .symptom-product-guide{margin-top:26px}.symptom-product-form,.symptom-product-result{padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-card);background:var(--card)}.symptom-product-form legend{font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);font-weight:700;line-height:1.25}.symptom-product-form fieldset{border:0;padding:0;margin:0}.symptom-product-form fieldset>p,.symptom-product-result>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:820px;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;line-height:1.7}.symptom-question-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:9px;margin:20px 0}.symptom-question-list label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:48px;padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;background:#fff;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;cursor:pointer}.symptom-question-list label:has(input:checked){border-color:var(--accent-sage);background:var(--accent-sky)}.symptom-question-list input{width:18px;height:18px;margin:0;accent-color:var(--accent-sage);flex:none}.symptom-question-list--quiet{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));margin-top:-10px}.symptom-product-result{margin-top:16px;background:#f7fbf8}.symptom-product-result h2{margin:5px 0 8px;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,32px)}.symptom-product-result .notice{margin:18px 0 0}.symptom-path-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin-top:20px}.symptom-path-grid article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:28px minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:16px;background:#fff}.symptom-path-grid article>span{display:grid;place-items:center;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent-sky);color:var(--accent-sage);font-weight:700}.symptom-path-grid .eyebrow{margin:1px 0 3px;font-size:9px}.symptom-path-grid h3{margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.35}.symptom-path-grid p:not(.eyebrow){margin:7px 0 10px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;line-height:1.55}.symptom-path-grid a{color:var(--accent-sage);font-size:12px;font-weight:700}.symptom-clinician-note{margin:18px 0 0;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);font-size:13px!important}.symptom-result-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;align-items:center;margin-top:16px}.symptom-result-actions .button{font-size:12px}.symptom-source-context{margin-top:18px;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:#fff}.symptom-source-context summary{font-weight:700}.symptom-source-context p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)}.symptom-source-context a{color:var(--link-color);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:700px){.symptom-question-list,.symptom-question-list--quiet,.symptom-path-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.symptom-product-form,.symptom-product-result{padding:18px}.symptom-question-list{margin:16px 0}.symptom-question-list--quiet{margin-top:-8px}}
  /* Keep every checkbox on the same axis, including multi-line questions. */
  .symptom-product-form {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .symptom-product-form legend {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .symptom-question-list {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .symptom-question-list label {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 18px minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: 12px;
    min-height: 46px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .symptom-question-list input {
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .symptom-question-list label:focus-within {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent-sage);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .symptom-question-list--quiet {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .symptom-question-list--quiet {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .symptom-question-list label {
      padding: 11px 12px;
      gap: 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
